  "title": "Prepositions and their cases",
  "description": "Which case follows each preposition, with its meaning and an example.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Every preposition takes a fixed case, and some take two with different meanings. W, na, pod, nad, przed and za take the accusative for movement towards a place, but the locative or instrumental for being there: Kładę książkę na stół (onto), but Książka leży na stole (on).",
      "table": {
        "columns": ["Preposition", "Case", "Meaning", "Example"],
        "rows": [
          ["do", "genitive", "to, into", "Idę do domu."],
          ["od", "genitive", "from (a person); since", "List od mamy."],
          ["z", "genitive", "from, out of", "Jestem z Polski."],
          ["bez", "genitive", "without", "Kawa bez cukru."],
          ["u", "genitive", "at someone's place", "Jestem u babci."],
          ["dla", "genitive", "for", "Prezent dla ciebie."],
          ["obok", "genitive", "next to", "Obok sklepu."],
          ["dzięki", "dative", "thanks to", "Dzięki tobie."],
          ["przez", "accusative", "through, across; for (time)", "Idę przez park."],
          ["na", "accusative", "onto; for (an event, a time)", "Idę na koncert."],
          ["z", "instrumental", "with", "Kawa z mlekiem."],
          ["nad", "instrumental", "above; by (water)", "Nad morzem."],
          ["pod", "instrumental", "under", "Pod stołem."],
          ["przed", "instrumental", "in front of; before", "Przed domem."],
          ["za", "instrumental", "behind", "Za domem."],
          ["między", "instrumental", "between", "Między nami."],
          ["w", "locative", "in", "W Krakowie."],
          ["na", "locative", "on; at", "Na poczcie."],
          ["o", "locative", "about", "O filmie."],
          ["przy", "locative", "by, near", "Przy oknie."],
          ["po", "locative", "after; around", "Po obiedzie."]
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
